    "updated_at": "2017-08-16T19:36:07Z",
    "body": "Great catch.\r\n\r\nDo you think preload is a special case here, or do you think we should apply the same logic for e.g. stylesheet, serviceworker, etc.?\r\n\r\nStylesheets have an interesting clause:\r\n\r\n> If element no longer creates an external resource link that contributes to the styling processing model, or if, since the resource in question was obtained, it has become appropriate to obtain it again (meaning this algorithm is about to be invoked again for a newly obtained resource), then abort these steps.\r\n\r\nThis doesn't tell us what should happen in terms of load vs. error event though; by omission it implies that the fetch should finish and the load event fire, even if the stylesheet doesn't apply.",
