    "created_at": "2017-08-23T05:20:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-23T05:20:13Z",
    "body": "I know that preload has a clear use-case for this: user action (e.g. mouse approaching a certain button) increases probability that a resource would be needed and therefore it is preloaded, but the user eventually performed a counter action (e.g. moved mouse away from button), so it's better to terminate preload if still possible.\r\n\r\nI don't know of a clear use-case for other link elements that download resources, but at the same time, if the element is removed from the DOM, seems better to avoid downloading it.",
